From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 00:41:42 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] wayland: Implement tearing-control-v1

Add the wp_tearing_control_manager_v1 global. get_tearing_control
creates a wp_tearing_control_v1 for a wl_surface (a second one is the
tearing_control_exists protocol error), set_presentation_hint records
vsync or async as double-buffered surface state applied on commit, and
destroying the object reverts the hint to vsync on the next commit. The
object goes inert when its surface is destroyed.

The hint is only recorded here. A new org.gnome.mutter "async-tearing"
setting (fullscreen-only by default, always, off) decides which surfaces
that ask for tearing get it; meta_wayland_tearing_control_get_policy()
exposes it to the compositor.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
